{
  "about": "Major roads by the names Google shows on a panorama's arrows, for the Map Generation Tool's filter \"Not on a major road\" and its tag (plan step 42). Written by hand from the owner's search logs of 13 November 2026 (ten logs, about 25 to 500 panoramas in each country) and OpenStreetMap's table of road classes by country (wiki.openstreetmap.org/wiki/Highway:International_equivalence). Major means OpenStreetMap's motorway, trunk and primary. For each country: \"major\", a regular expression for the name of a major road (matched against the whole name Google shows); \"roads\", what counts, in words, for the help; \"partly\": true where the names tell only motorways and trunk roads apart, so only those count; and examples from the logs, which the build checks (\"major\" must match, \"other\" must not). Google sometimes writes a letter in Cyrillic that looks like a Latin one (М-4 and M-4, Р-255 and P27), so the patterns of such countries take both. The page matches them in JavaScript, where \\b only knows Latin letters: after a letter of another script, a pattern says what follows (a space, a digit or the end) instead.",
